
# CloudWin Deployment

## Requirements

- Ubuntu Server 24.04
- QEMU/KVM
- Libvirt
- 8 GB RAM minimum for the VM
- Windows installation ISO
- Valid Windows licence

## 1. Install virtualization packages

```bash
sudo apt update

sudo apt install -y \
  qemu-kvm \
  libvirt-daemon-system \
  libvirt-clients \
  virtinst \
  qemu-utils \
  cpu-checker \
  python3 \
  python3-venv \
  git
```

## 2. Enable virtualization

```bash
sudo systemctl enable --now libvirtd
kvm-ok
```

## 3. Download CloudWin

```bash
git clone YOUR-REPOSITORY-URL
cd CloudWin
sudo ./scripts/install.sh
```

## 4. Configure CloudWin

```bash
sudo cp /opt/cloudwin/config.env.example /opt/cloudwin/config.env
sudo nano /opt/cloudwin/config.env
```

## 5. Add Windows ISO

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /var/lib/cloudwin/iso
```

Copy your legally obtained Windows ISO to:

`/var/lib/cloudwin/iso/windows.iso`

## 6. Create the virtual machine

```bash
sudo /opt/cloudwin/scripts/create-vm.sh
```

## 7. Start the services

```bash
sudo systemctl enable --now cloudwin-web
sudo systemctl enable --now cloudwin-novnc
sudo virsh start cloudwin
```

## 8. Connect securely

Use SSH port forwarding:

```bash
ssh -N \
  -L 8080:127.0.0.1:8080 \
  -L 6080:127.0.0.1:6080 \
  USERNAME@SERVER-IP
```

Open `http://127.0.0.1:8080` in your browser.
